From: PowerVLC
Subject: [PATCH] configure: use FSF GCC AltiVec flags and header on Darwin
 PowerPC

x264 assumes that every Darwin PowerPC compiler is Apple GCC and forces
-faltivec -fastf -mcpu=G4.  PowerVLC cross-builds the legacy slices with
FSF GCC 13, which rejects all three Apple spellings.  Unlike Apple GCC,
FSF GCC also exposes the vec_* intrinsics through <altivec.h>.  The contrib
driver already supplies the selected CPU and tuning flags; add only the
portable AltiVec ABI flags and enable the standard header.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -799,7 +799,8 @@ case $host_cpu in
             AS="${AS-${CC}}"
             AS_EXT=".c"
             if [ $SYS = MACOSX ] ; then
-                CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -faltivec -fastf -mcpu=G4"
+                CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -maltivec -mabi=altivec"
+                define HAVE_ALTIVEC_H
             else
                 CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -maltivec -mabi=altivec"
                 define HAVE_ALTIVEC_H
